{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Proposed repair (production write, NOT performed; awaiting operator approval). Run on the host via SSM against the live MCP container; every step is guarded and stops on the first failure:\n\n```\nC=$(docker ps --format '{{.Names}}' | grep '^rebar-mcp' | head -1)\ndocker exec \"$C\" sh -c 'cd \"$MCP_CODE_DIR\" &&\n  git diff --cached --quiet e2ed08b343a2be462de4433a93edbb5cbc062a52 &&\n  git diff --quiet &&\n  test -z \"$(git ls-files --others --exclude-standard)\" &&\n  git update-ref -m \"repair interrupted fast-forward\" HEAD e2ed08b343a2be462de4433a93edbb5cbc062a52 3835269d792b7764e0beeca95798250487c78895 &&\n  test -z \"$(git status --porcelain)\" &&\n  git fetch origin main && git merge --ff-only origin/main &&\n  git rev-list --left-right --count HEAD...origin/main'\n```\n\nWhy this is safe: the first 3 checks prove the index and working tree already ARE e2ed08b343a and nothing else; update-ref is compare-and-swap against the current HEAD, so it only moves the branch onto the tree already on disk (no file is rewritten, nothing is discarded). After that the tree is clean and the runbook's own break-glass fast-forward (review-bot-ops.md \"MCP code workspace freshness\") applies. Expected final line `0 0`. Then re-run the read-only in-container resolution: frontier/standard/trivial should read opus-5-5 / sonnet-5-5 / haiku-5-5. load_config re-stats rebar.toml on each call, so no restart is expected to be needed; that is unverified until the resolution check runs."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794363688699780194,"uuid":"6606d28c-90a8-4337-b35a-5d02736f92f2"}